 "reports_individuals_with_tnfaip3_variant": true,
 "relevance_note": "A narrative review of autoinflammatory skin diseases whose only individual-level Blau syndrome content is the Fig. 6 legend describing two boys (\"A 12-year-old boy with disseminated small scaly solid papules\"; \"A 4-year-old boy showing joint involvement\"); no NOD2 variant is given for any person.",
 "method_note": "Read the whole Markdown by hand (body, Table I and references; no supplementary section). Table I and the text describe Blau syndrome only at disease level and give no individuals. The only in-scope people are the two boys pictured in Fig. 6 (panels A and B) under the heading 'Blau syndrome'; the paper gives them no labels, so they are 'unnamed person 1' and 'unnamed person 2' (rule 6; panel letters label images, not people). Their ages are taken as age at the time of the photograph (age_at_last_evaluation). The 6-month onset is stated for the skin eruptions of person 1 only, so it is recorded as feature onset, not as age at disease onset. The paper does not say these boys were genetically tested, so no variant rows. Person 2's 'joint involvement with cystic swelling of the dorsal sides of the left hand' is kept as a feature row, but the arthritis and tenosynovitis checklist items are left 'not reported' because the legend names neither. No contradictions found. A script assembled the JSON from hand-chosen values and spans.",
